lted/397623-abyssal-working-for-non-deathlords?p=398387#post398387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> &quot;LOVER! LET'S SEE YOU GRIT THOSE TEETH!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=qmEJbALlz3g\" data-code=\"qmEJbALlz3g\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/qmEJbALlz3g/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-08T22:26:27-08:00","id":398453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/397623-abyssal-working-for-non-deathlords?p=398295#post398295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Abyssals have never really been the Deathlord's lapdogs-on-demand. In fact, I seem to recall the developers being fairly open during both editions about the fact that the Deathlords are training their replacements and they don't even know it.</div> </div> </div> </div>On an individual basis that's essentially meaningless. The Abyssals may replace the Deathlords eventually, but that hardly matters to the Abyssals on the recieving end of a capricious 'You Have Failed Me' moment. Then after that you work directly for the Neverborn which as Immortal Malevolence Enslavement shows us is even worse, you can't even be the psychopath who only enjoys killing anymore.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/397623-abyssal-working-for-non-deathlords?p=398295#post398295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(I'm somewhat ambivalent about that. On the one hand, Abyssals should probably not be like Prometheans, where they can't ever rest in one place very long without tearing it down around them. On the other hand, the Neverborn probably would include <i>some</i> sort of mechanism by which they can be very, very sure that the Abyssals are always going to do their jobs, being as how the Neverborn went down the road of &quot;let's imbue some servitors with vast powers and only minimally functional leashes&quot; and the end result of that was &quot;said servitors murdered the fuck out of us and now we're the Neverborn.&quot;)</div> </div> </div> </div>What the Neverborn would want is irrelevant even if we assume they're fully fledged actors rather than tomb bodies that occasionally groan something meaningful. <br /> They have stolen Exaltations that just might not accept certain paramiters and their means to alter them came from the Yozis, who even if we assume acted in completely good faith despite incompatible long-term goals have failed spectacularly in their attempts to leash their own servants.<br /> The simple fact that Abyssals can be returned to Solars is far more destructive to their long-term plans than 100+ Abyssals doing whatever they want save for the limitations of their charmset.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>success is the ability to go from one failure to the next without any loss of enthusiasm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1115-the-hug-ninja","name":"The Hug Ninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1115_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"324"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-08T23:19:28-08:00","id":398474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Hug Ninja</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/397623-abyssal-working-for-non-deathlords?p=398453#post398453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On an individual basis that's essentially meaningless. The Abyssals may replace the Deathlords eventually, but that hardly matters to the Abyssals on the recieving end of a capricious 'You Have Failed Me' moment.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does your Abyssal have to stick around to be Vader-choked if they don't want to? Because as I recall, they don't. They can decide that their Deathlord sucks and bail out of their service and short of actually hunting them down, the Deathlord can't do a damn thing about it. (I may be wrong about this. I seem to recall that the Deathlords have an extreme sanction on-hand. Something involving destroying the Monstrance? But I recall that had a huge downside for all involved.)<br /> <br /> Unless the Deathlords can somehow enforce loyalty by thinking about it, their Abyssals are no more their &quot;on demand&quot; lapdogs than a Dragon-Blooded in the Vermillion Legion is the Roseblacks &quot;on demand&quot; lapdog. They can always pick up stakes and head out on their own. That might get them killed, mind you, but that's the flip side of being part of a larger society.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What the Neverborn would want is irrelevant even if we assume they're fully fledged actors rather than tomb bodies that occasionally groan something meaningful. </div> </div> </div>In the context of 2e, we don't have to &quot;assume&quot; that. They explicitly are conducting complex diplomacy with the Yozi's and disciplining their subordinates in concrete, logical fashion. I would submit that that's fairly dispositive.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They have stolen Exaltations that just might not accept certain paramiters and their means to alter them came from the Yozis, who even if we assume acted in completely good faith despite incompatible long-term goals have failed spectacularly in their attempts to leash their own servants.<br /> The simple fact that Abyssals can be returned to Solars is far more destructive to their long-term plans than 100+ Abyssals doing whatever they want save for the limitations of their charmset. </div> </div> </div>I do take your larger point that the Neverborn can only twist the Solar shards so far, and that you can use this to justify a lot of limitations on their control over the Abyssals.<br /> <br /> However, there comes a point where it would be breathtakingly stupid for them to deploy those shards if they can't exercise some degree of perceived control over them. You reference the Yozis and their failed leashing. But the Yozi's did <i>try to</i> leash them, and that leash makes sense within the context of Malfeas and how he thinks, which is that yelling and screaming and beating people up is the way you enforce obedience to his perfected Tyranny.<br /> <br /> I don't see the Neverborn deploying the Abyssals without an attempt at a control mechanism. Given what happened the last time they tried that it seems like they'd go &quot;No. No way, no how. We'll simply sit on these shards for eternity rather than rolling <i>those</i> bones again.&quot;<br /> <br /> That said, the control mechanism should be a hell of a lot more fun to interact with than the 2e control mechanism was. Now, from a narrative standpoint? The 2e control mechanism was a thing of sublime beauty. &quot;You're going to destroy the world for us. No, really, you are. It literally doesn't matter what you do. It's baked into your being. No complaining! You signed up for this, and no backsies. You can try and run if you want, but in the end you'll do what we want. <i>It's in your nature</i>.&quot;<br /> <br /> The downside was that it wasn't <i>fun</i>. It wasn't interesting to interact with. There was no way to make it work for you or to trick or stunt your way around it, and unlike the Limit Breaks it was really hard to embrace it in a productive way.<br /> <br /> That, I submit, is the part that has to be fixed. I know a lot of people really want Abyssals to be completely free as a bird and be able to fuck off away from the Neverborn's agenda with no consequence, but I've always found that idea to be both illogical from an in-setting standpoint and something of a cop-out from a meta standpoint. You're playing a weapon aimed at the throat of the world. Your character <i>agreed</i> to be a weapon aimed at the throat of the world. That should carry a more meaningful weight to it than &quot;you get awesome death powers that have no downside.&quot; If you don't want to play a weapon aimed at the throat of the world, perhaps Abyssals are not the splat for you.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T00:13:35-08:00","id":398523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/397623-abyssal-working-for-non-deathlords?p=398474#post398474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(I may be wrong about this. I seem to recall that the Deathlords have an extreme sanction on-hand. Something involving destroying the Monstrance? But I recall that had a huge downside for all involved.)</div> </div> </div> </div> You are.<br /> The Monstance is an Arcane Link for the purposes of Necromancy and certain Abyssal charms, they can torture and even kill you from the other side of the world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>success is the ability to go from one failure to the next without any loss of enthusiasm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1115-the-hug-ninja","name":"The Hug Ninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1115_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"324"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T00:19:57-08:00","id":398541,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Does your Abyssal have to stick around to be Vader-choked if they don't want to? Because as I recall, they don't. They can decide that their Deathlord sucks and bail out of their service and short of actually hunting them down, the Deathlord can't do a damn thing about it. (I may be wrong about this. I seem to recall that the Deathlords have an extreme sanction on-hand. Something involving destroying the Monstrance? But I recall that had a huge downside for all involved.) </div> </div> </div>When it was released they totally could just insta-kill you with no possibility of a saving throw no matter where you were and then use a third circle necromancy spell to retrieve your exaltation and bind it to a replacement Monstrance This was later errata'd on the grounds of being totally ****ing stupid even compared to 2E resonance mechanics.<br /> <br /> Edit: Oh, wait, the book also says it destroys your exaltation. But everything else treats exaltations as being immune to Oblivion so that didn't need to be undone by the scroll of errata.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":988,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","user":"Mizu","date":". 02-09-2015, 03:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T00:37:38-08:00","id":398550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/397623-abyssal-working-for-non-deathlords?p=398474#post398474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, there comes a point where it would be breathtakingly stupid for them to deploy those shards if they can't exercise some degree of perceived control over them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why? What are they going to do? Kill them <i>again</i>?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-li