n-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/397623-abyssal-working-for-non-deathlords?p=398474#post398474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> However, there comes a point where it would be breathtakingly stupid for them to deploy those shards if they can't exercise some degree of perceived control over them.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Let them go if they want to go; let them be free. Eventually, they will bring darkness to the world, as surely as we, the Solars once did.&quot;<br /> \u2014The Bodhisattva Anointed by Dark Waters<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T05:23:53-08:00","id":398678,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/397623-abyssal-working-for-non-deathlords?p=398550#post398550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why? What are they going to do? Kill them <i>again</i>?</div> </div> </div> </div>well they did kill them and that is supposed to be impossible to do so it's pretty logical that they keep some sort of &quot;do not break the rules of the universe on my face again&quot; safety precaution","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm making the Tales of Exalts webcomic<br /> <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/50854781/tales-of-exalts\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...ales-of-exalts</a><br /> alchemical report <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/54812164/Alchemical-Report\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...hemical-Report</a><br /> the fall <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4455-xanroth","name":"Xanroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4455_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1072"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T06:49:08-08:00","id":398739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xanroth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/397623-abyssal-working-for-non-deathlords?p=398678#post398678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">well they did kill them and that is supposed to be impossible to do so it's pretty logical that they keep some sort of &amp;quot;do not break the rules of the universe on my face again&amp;quot; safety precaution</div> </div> </div> </div> Unless they really want to die for real, and not just sort-of half die like what happened last time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T08:35:31-08:00","id":398793,"title":"","content":"Okay, so. apparently, I can't read. Aside from it being a complete failure of my information-handling skills in general, it means I've run no less than two games completely wrongly and they didn't turn out the way they should have, from my perspective.<br /> <br /> I mean... wow. That idea is just so bad I must have blocked it out. I absolutely stand by my opinion there should be a leash mechanism, but giving that kind of absolute whip hand to the Deathlords is insane. It's unfun and of dubious utility from a playability standpoint and more to the point can't be engaged with constructively. Is every single Abyssal that wants to go rogue supposed to orchestrate a Monstrance heist? (Monstrance heists are pretty cool, but... every time?) That's idiotic.<br /> <br /> Regardless. I was wrong on the facts. That's on me. I'll try to do better. I withdraw all comments about Abyssals being lapdogs-on-demand, as they... kind of are.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Why? What are they going to do? Kill them <i>again</i>? </div> </div> </div>One of the constants of Creation is that things can always get worse.<br /> <br /> But more seriously, the Neverborn would presumably prefer their agenda be advanced. Loosing a bunch of Solar shards, even tainted ones, into the world with no guarantee they'll do that seems like it is a dubious proposition, especially since those shards will be bound to people who are suddenly near-immortal fonts of power. You know what near-immortal fonts of power like to do? Keep on existing so they can exercise that power in ways pleasing to them. Taking action to preserve Creation (in which I include the Underworld) runs squarely counter to the Neverborns agenda.<br /> <br /> If I were a Neverborn, I would be thinking &quot;sending these guys out without some sort of mechanism to at least sort of guarantee they'll do as we want means that there's a good chance our tombs will eventually be hooked into some sort of awful, terrifying Death/Life Engine designed to turn our own power against ourselves and preserve their endless Empires of the Dead and Damned.&quot;<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;Let them go if they want to go; let them be free. Eventually, they will bring darkness to the world, as surely as we, the Solars once did.&quot;<br /> \u2014The Bodhisattva Anointed by Dark Waters </div> </div> </div>The Silver Prince is a pseudo-intellectual douchenozzle. But aside from that, his statement is only true in the context he made it, in which the Neverborn did, in fact, build in a mechanism to guarantee that the Abyssals would work that way.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Unless they really want to die for real, and not just sort-of half die like what happened last time. </div> </div> </div>Well, in fairness, they'd be thrilled if that happened. The Neverborn want to properly die. That's the whole point of their agenda, really. They would like to drop into Oblivion and <i>end</i>. If an Abyssal came to the Neverborn and told them he could kill them for real, he would be honored as no other before him, and bestowed with great blessings of power and gratitude as he ushered his patrons one by one into a true death.<br /> <hr /><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T09:42:50-08:00","id":398902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/397623-abyssal-working-for-non-deathlords?p=398541#post398541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> When it was released they totally could just insta-kill you with no possibility of a saving throw no matter where you were and then use a third circle necromancy spell to retrieve your exaltation and bind it to a replacement Monstrance This was later errata'd on the grounds of being totally ****ing stupid even compared to 2E resonance mechanics.<br /> <br /> Edit: Oh, wait, the book also says it destroys your exaltation. But everything else treats exaltations as being immune to Oblivion so that didn't need to be undone by the scroll of errata.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Wait, which book? 2E Abyssals says, on page 116, that &quot;Abyssals feel the destruction of thier Monstrances as a breath of hope, regaining all willpower points.&quot; Shortly after, it brings up the possibility of killing Deathknights via the Monstrance Arcane Link, but points out that Deathlords rarely do this, because it frees the Exaltation that might then be poached by another Deathlord.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T09:58:42-08:00","id":398967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> because it frees the Exaltation that might then be poached by another Deathlord. </div> </div> </div>Calling the Black Sun let the Deathlord re-capture the Abyssal Exaltation and stuff it inside another Monstrance, I think the spell has been errata though.<br /> <br /> And I hope that the Neverborn won't be so micro-management and remotely affect so many things in Third Edition, aren't they suppose to be dead Primordials, not Primordials with death theme ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":298,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","user":"Jen","date":". 02-09-2015, 01:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T11:27:50-08:00","id":399076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/397623-abyssal-working-for-non-deathlords?p=398902#post398902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Wait, which book? 2E Abyssals says, on page 116, that &quot;Abyssals feel the destruction of thier Monstrances as a breath of hope, regaining all willpower points.&quot; Shortly after, it brings up the possibility of killing Deathknights via the Monstrance Arcane Link, but points out that Deathlords rarely do this, because it frees the Exaltation that might then be poached by another Deathlord.</div> </div> </div> </div>Manual of Exalted Power: The Abyssals, page 42<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In the worst-case scenarios, however, a Deathlord can<br /> deliver a punishment whence there is no return and no hope<br /> of forgiveness. If a deathknight truly enrages his master,<br /> the Deathlord can hurl the doomed failure\u2019s Monstrance of<br /> Celestial Portion into the Abyss, destroying the deathknight<br /> utterly, Exaltation and all. </div> </div> </div>Also, Fallen Wolf of the Cutting Sea's write up in that book centers heavily on him feeling helpless to really rebel against his master because he will just instantly die if he does so.<br /> <br /> So, yeah, I guess Oblivion's super death powers kill you via the arcane link that also lets people use it to smack you with spells and stuff?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T12:02:22-08:00","id":399124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">But aside from that, his statement is only true in the context he made it</div> </div> </div> </div> The context is Third Edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T12:32:47-08:00","id":399178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/397623-abyssal-working-for-non-deathlords?p=399124#post399124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The context is Third Edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>... which doesn't have any mechanical information about the Abyssals out yet. Like, at all. I don't think even to playtesters.<br /> <br /> I will therefore give the Silver Princes' pontificating all the weight it deserves.<br /> <br /> (I am curious as to the provenance of that quote, though. Is it in the playtest materiel, or someplace where those of us not in the playtest can actually access it? Is there wider context or is it just a single line?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T12:39:50-08:00","id":399184,"title":"","content":"It deserves the weight of the developers telling us what the design and style priorities are for the Abyssal Exalted, in particular with regards to somebody who might question why the Deathlords would tolerate the existence of Abyssals over whom they do not have direct means of leashing. Jesus Christ...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T13:40:00-08:00","id":399236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/397623-abyssal-working-for-non-deathlords?p=399184#post399184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It deserves the weight of the developers telling us what the design and style priorities are for the Abyssal Exalted</div> </div> </div> </div>I was unaware that the Silver Prince was a line developer!<br /> <br /> Without a lot more context than you've given, all that quote tells us is how the Silver Prince views letting Abyssals run wild and free. That's it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T13:43:49-08:00","id":399239,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/397623-abyssal-working-for-non-deathlords?p=399076#post399076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Manual of Exalted Power: The Abyssals, page 42<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Also, Fallen Wolf of the Cutting Sea's write up in that book centers heavily on him feeling helpless to really rebel against his master because he will just instantly die if he does so.<br /> <br /> So, yeah, I guess Oblivion's super death powers kill you via the arcane link that also lets people use it to smack you with spells and stuff?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hand of Omega's quote was errata aimed at the stupid Monstrance killswitch. It is admittedly pretty confusing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T13:50:40-08:00","id":399244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was unaware that the Silver Prince was a line developer!</div> </div> </div> </div> I'm going to be generous and assume this is not sophistry, so: that was a line written by John in the course of a discussion of Third Edition Abyssals and some distinctions of what their relationship with the Deathlords being more aprentice than slave was.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T13:58:58-08:00","id":399266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/397623-abyssal-working-for-non-deathlords?p=399239#post399239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hand of Omega's quote was errata aimed at the stupid Monstrance killswitch. It is admittedly pretty confusing.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm pretty sure my PDF doesn't have errata incorporated, and it does indeed say that a Monstrance being destroyed makes an abyssal feel awesome (except, apparently, if it is destroyed in one specific way).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Durability: 30A/30L/30B soak; 50 levels of damage<br /> needed to bend the bars or break a hole wide enough for an<br /> adult human to squeeze through and 100 levels of damage to<br /> destroy completely. No magic can harm them in any way. The<br /> cages are equally solid to dematerialized beings and require<br /> a (Strength + Athletics) total of 20 or more to lift. They<br /> are harder to move than they look. Damaged Monstrances<br /> mend themselves at the rate of one level per hour. Only the<br /> Monstrance\u2019s owner can open the hinged doors on one side,<br /> and the doors resist any \u201copening\u201d magic. Abyssals feel the<br /> destruction of their Monstrances as a breath of hope, regaining<br /> all willpower points. </div> </div> </div>I'm thinking that maybe this was one of those cases where certain writers working on the book didn't like what the guy in charge of the book was going for, it would explain why part of the ST section suggested just saying the Deathlords were full of **** and couldn't actually kill you by tossing the Monstrance into Oblivion if your group wanted to run a renegade abyssal game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":988,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","user":"Mizu","date":". 02-09-2015, 05:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T14:05:01-08:00","id":399302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/397623-abyssal-working-for-non-deathlords?p=399266#post399266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I'm pretty sure my PDF doesn't have errata incorporated, and it does indeed say that a Monstrance being destroyed makes an abyssal feel awesome (except, apparently, if it is destroyed in one specific way).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I'm thinking that maybe this was one of those cases where certain writers working on the book didn't like what the guy in charge of the book was going for, it would explain why part of the ST section suggested just saying the Deathlords were full of **** and couldn't actually kill you by tossing the Monstrance into Oblivion if your group wanted to run a renegade abyssal game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Apparently it is <i>even more confusing</i> than I had assumed. Christ.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T14:06:32-08:00","id":399306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/397623-abyssal-working-for-non-deathlords?p=399244#post399244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I'm going to be generous and assume this is not sophistry, so: that was a line written by John in the course of a discussion of Third Edition Abyssals and some distinctions of what their relationship with the Deathlords being more aprentice than slave was.</div> </div> </div> </div>It wasn't, intended as sophistry, no. You tossed that quote out as if an in-setting piece of dialogue from a certifiably batshit insane dude was somehow dispositive, with no further context or explication. Hence the two times, one implied, one explicit, I asked for context.<br /> <br /> That said: I basically take it as a given that 3e Abyssals won't have a brutal choke chain attached to their necks, or a Resonance mechanic (if indeed Resonance is still a thing at all) that's as unfun to engage with as it was in 2e. (1e Resonance could at least be gamed in fun and interesting ways if you knew what you were doing.)<br /> <br /> What I hope is that they still have some sort of interesting mechanic that ensures or attempts to ensure that they do what the Neverborn want'em to do. This is partly because of verisimilitude, which is important to me as a player and as a GM, and partly because aesthetically speaking I really hate the idea that you can sign onto Team Nihilism, get awesome death powers and pseudo-immortality, and there not be really, really powerful strings attached.<br /> <br /> I will be signficantly more ambivalent about this point if in 3e you don't choose to become an Abyssal, it's something that happens TO you, like Solar/Lunar/Sidereal does. That changes the calculus of game design and narrative weight considerably in my view.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T14:13:35-08:00","id":399314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/397623-abyssal-working-for-non-deathlords?p=399302#post399302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Apparently it is <i>even more confusing</i> than I had assumed. Christ.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sure that everyone would like to forget how bad that book was.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T16:02:42-08:00","id":399492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/397623-abyssal-working-for-non-deathlords?p=399306#post399306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It wasn't, intended as sophistry, no. You tossed that quote out as if an in-setting piece of dialogue from a certifiably batshit insane dude was somehow dispositive, with no further context or explication. Hence the two times, one implied, one explicit, I asked for context.<br /> <br /> That said: I basically take it as a given that 3e Abyssals won't have a brutal choke chain attached to their necks, or a Resonance mechanic (if indeed Resonance is still a thing at all) that's as unfun to engage with as it was in 2e. (1e Resonance could at least be gamed in fun and interesting ways if you knew what you were doing.)<br /> <br /> What I hope is that they still have some sort of interesting mechanic that ensures or attempts to ensure that they do what the Neverborn want'em to do. This is partly because of verisimilitude, which is important to me as a player and as a GM, and partly because aesthetically speaking I really hate the idea that you can sign onto Team Nihilism, get awesome death powers and pseudo-immortality, and there not be really, really powerful strings attached.<br /> <br /> I will be signficantly more ambivalent about this point if in 3e you don't choose to become an Abyssal, it's something that happens TO you, like Solar/Lunar/Sidereal does. That changes the calculus of game design and narrative weight considerably in my view.</div> </div> </div> </div>It may help to consider that the Deathlords and Neverborn* are coming at everything from a very skewed set of perspectives. The Deathlords were once the betrayed lords and masters of the First Age: they know full well what Solars are capable of doing and being. They've had centuries of reflection as ghosts in dead lands to tint those memories in a very cynical direction, to boot. This is going to impact their outlook and what they perceive as necessary. That, to my understanding, is where they get the sentiment in that John M\u00f8rke quote Isator dropped in earlier.<br /> <br /> * I'd honestly not be surprised if the Neverborn were more-or-less not a part of the decision-making process. A search for particular quotes fails me, but the members of the EX3 Team haven't historically sounded too keen on the Neverborn as direct actors, to my recollection.<br /> <br /> There's also the question of whether putting in a &quot;control mechanism&quot; was even in the cards. Well, aside from the control mechanism that was always there, &quot;Choose Abyssal candidates with care.&quot; I gotta be honest, I don't think that one's to be neglected. I think there's a strong chance of everything cohering together for you, though I don't know your precise tastes.<br /> <br /> You may find some interesting reading in the <a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/ExaltedWiki/mediawiki-1.19.1/index.php?title=Exalts#Abyssals\" target=\"_blank\">Abyssal section</a> (and <a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/ExaltedWiki/mediawiki-1.19.1/index.php?title=Exalted_3E:_What_We_Know#Deathlords\" target=\"_blank\">Deathlord section</a>) of the EX3 What We Know Wiki. Here are some relevant bits.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Abyssals in 3e are deathknights. They are emissaries, heralds, and famulii, but not slaves. They have a Deathlord/apprentice relationship. They are not murdermachines or killbots; they do not have a Resonance which forces them to kill or kills for them. You will be able to strike out from the Deathlord's shadow. They intended you to do so, because they think that you will most certainly end up killing Creation even if you decide to be a hero. This is a legitimate claim when you consider that they were once Solars, and Solars in the late First Age were one fit of pique away from doing irreversible harm to Creation.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holden</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">3e Resonance is a very different beast from either the 2e hardback version, or the Doom found in Shards. I'm pretty excited about it.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EX3 What We Know Wiki</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Q: MiltonSlavemasta</b><br /> Do all the Deathlords seek to end the world?<br /> <br /> <b>A: </b><b>Holden</b><br /> They're supposed to-- but they tend to have their own ideas about what to do with a deathless eternity stretching out before them.<br /> <br /> ... <b>Q: </b><b>emeraldstreak</b><br /> Still unsure what the Deathlords will consider a victory though. Dragging everyone in Oblivion? Avenging the Usurpation? Giving Creation the taste of torment they've suffered?<br /> <br /> <b>A: </b><b>Holden</b><br /> 13 individuals, 13 different desires.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Demented One</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">To re-rail this topic, I think I'll set that there are going to be many differences in how Deathlords are presented and conceptualized in Third Edition, and one of the effects of this is that they might be people you <i>want</i> to be the knights of, even if you aren't a sadistic killer or a true believer. For example, I've got a concept kicking around for an Abyssal loyal to the Dowager, but whose deeds in Creation earn them a heroic reputation, and rightly so. Instead of &quot;serve the Deathlords&quot; being one pole of your spectrum of play options, it's an entire spectrum unto itself (plus all the possibilities of being independent).</div> </div> </div> </div></div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T16:25:15-08:00","id":399501,"title":"","content":"I still have no idea what a famulii is, putting it into Google gives me links to profiles of people on what seem to be a foreign knock off of facebook, something which mentions groups of a certain kind of animal are called famuli, and a lot of stuff that might be useful but I can't read whatever language they are written in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T16:30:32-08:00","id":399502,"title":"","content":"Actually, while a dev is watching this thread... is an Abyssal turning their Exaltation back to a Solar one still a valid option in 3e?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1596-horngeek","name":"horngeek","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T16:57:15-08:00","id":399567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/397623-abyssal-working-for-non-deathlords?p=398793#post398793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I were a Neverborn, I would be thinking &quot;sending these guys out without some sort of mechanism to at least sort of guarantee they'll do as we want means that there's a good chance our tombs will eventually be hooked into some sort of awful, terrifying Death/Life Engine designed to turn our own power against ourselves and preserve their endless Empires of the Dead and Damned.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>As I understand it, if you were a Neverborn, you would be thinking, &quot;AAAAaaaaAAAApainAAAAaaaaAAAAagonyAAAARGH&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T17:06:33-08:00","id":399575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/397623-abyssal-working-for-non-deathlords?p=399306#post399306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said: I basically take it as a given that 3e Abyssals won't have a brutal choke chain attached to their necks, or a Resonance mechanic (if indeed Resonance is still a thing at all) that's as unfun to engage with as it was in 2e. (1e Resonance could at least be gamed in fun and interesting ways if you knew what you were doing.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll note that the concept of &quot;gaming&quot; Resonance sure isn't playing into the RAI of what Resonance is supposed to be, just like &quot;gaming&quot; Limit should really be a Thing since you're getting something positive from a state intended to be incredibly negative.<br /> <br /> There should be some interesting medium between &quot;this is a curse I can subvert for Fun and Profit&quot; and &quot;this is a behaviorally-restrictive mechanic which effectively plays my character for me, and that's bullshit.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T17:25:09-08:00","id":399608,"title":"","content":"Dipping back to the thread topic, I'd definitely be interested in seeing a death knight who's chosen service to a raksha lord. Especially if Abyssals still have a fair bit of stuff in the vein of &quot;All Dreams Die,&quot; and are otherwise seen by the Fair Folk as harbingers of hated stasis, it would potentially be a... contentious relationship. Still, even just from a material perspective, they may have more to offer each other than it seems. The raksha would certainly delight in having such an ace in the hole when making war on his fellows or the hannya, or in bringing especially mighty behemoths to heel, while the Abyssal might receive rarefied wonders capable of things and methods he finds difficult with his native magics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T17:33:51-08:00","id":399612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/397623-abyssal-working-for-non-deathlords?p=399567#post399567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I understand it, if you were a Neverborn, you would be thinking, &quot;AAAAaaaaAAAApainAAAAaaaaAAAAagonyAAAARGH&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm interested in seeing how the Deathlords got their power if the Neverborn can do little more then writhe in their agony laced slumber.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T19:24:58-08:00","id":399776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/397623-abyssal-working-for-non-deathlords?p=399567#post399567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I understand it, if you were a Neverborn, you would be thinking, &quot;AAAAaaaaAAAApainAAAAaaaaAAAAagonyAAAARGH&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>That's deeply and incredibly boring, if true. I'm okay with the Neverborn not just being a pack of death-inflected Primordials, and I'm even okay with (and it would be awesome) a whole thing where people are unsure about stuff like &quot;how much of what I learned down in the Labyrinth is the true will of my dark patrons, and how much is my brain cracking in their presence and making up its own shit.&quot;<br /> <br /> But they should still be action drivers, I think. They should have an agenda and be acting towards it, even if that agenda is clouded by pain, rage, and insanity. Perhaps that's just me; I've always liked the Neverborn, with their tomb-slumber and urge towards ending their suffering the only way they know how, to be a lot more interesting and engaging than the Deathlords, who have their upsides but who, as the thread said, have always been vaguely &quot;Skeletors 1-13.&quot; I kept hoping word count would one day be spent on them. And I always tend to prefer beings that <i>do</i> over beings that <i>are</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/397623-abyssal-working-for-non-deathlords?p=399575#post399575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll note that the concept of &quot;gaming&quot; Resonance sure isn't playing into the RAI of what Resonance is supposed to be, just like &quot;gaming&quot; Limit should really be a Thing since you're getting something positive from a state intended to be incredibly negative.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not, no, but both implementations have been sufficiently clunky that it's one of your only options to have fun with it.<br /> <br /> The behavior mechanics should be fun. Now, this is of course one of the historically hot topics and some people are never, ever going to find behavior mechanics fun. I used to be of that opinion, before I learned to find the fun and excitement of really embracing a Limit Break and riding it all the way through to its wreckage-strewn end. But I haven't met a lot of people who find Resonance in its intended forms all that much fun to play around, and I've gamed with people who loved playing Prometheans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T20:37:15-08:00","id":399901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/397623-abyssal-working-for-non-deathlords?p=399266#post399266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm thinking that maybe this was one of those cases where certain writers working on the book didn't like what the guy in charge of the book was going for, it would explain why part of the ST section suggested just saying the Deathlords were full of **** and couldn't actually kill you by tossing the Monstrance into Oblivion if your group wanted to run a renegade abyssal game.</div> </div> </div> </div>And page 42 says that if an Abyssal's Monstrance is tossed into Oblivion the Abyssal dies. <br /> <br /> I remember Neph discussing this not too long after Abyssals came out. What happened was, it had been recognized that the Abyssal Killswitch was dumb back in First Edition, and when 2nd edition was being written, it was planned to remove it. Abyssal killswitch was no longer supposed to be a thing. So Neph wrote in the book about the Monstrance's destruction restoring an Abyssal's willpower, because that's how it was supposed to work. Unfortunately there were some communication issues, the authors working on Chapter One and Seven hadn't been informed that this was changing, so they mentioned the Abyssal killswitch (even using that direct term in Chapter 7), and it wasn't caught in final editing.<br /> <br /> So we ended up with two rules - the one in Chapter One/Seven, which says and Abyssal dies if his monstrance is throwing into Oblivion, and the other rule in Chapter 4 that said the Abyssal regains his willpower when his monstrance is destroyed. But it was intended that Chapter 4 be the official statement on what happened when you destroyed a Monstrance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T20:45:19-08:00","id":399908,"title":"","content":"Ah, so it was a miscommunication as opposed to deliberately contradicting the intent of the guy in charge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T22:38:46-08:00","id":400006,"title":"","content":"I'm gonna dissect this post a bit, but please don't read in too much hostility.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/397623-abyssal-working-for-non-deathlords?p=399306#post399306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You tossed that quote out as if an in-setting piece of dialogue from a certifiably batshit insane dude was somehow dispositive, with no further context or explication.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's strange that you discount Silver Prince's perspective as madness but hold the Neverborn to such a high standard. If he's crazy, what are they? He's at least in some contact with reality and capable of remembering or interacting with humankind, since he's not an ancient inhuman intelligence trapped in darkness and perpetual agony, so he's got that goin' for him. I don't expect beings like the Neverborn to approach their problems in ways I would understand or approve of.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/397623-abyssal-working-for-non-deathlords?p=399306#post399306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I hope is that they still have some sort of interesting mechanic that ensures or attempts to ensure that they do what the Neverborn want'em to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dark powers taught by dark masters go a long way, so I'm cool with a light touch here. For example, we accept that Solars will generally shake things up - there aren't a lot of threads positing that the large majority of Solars might just ignore their potential and twiddle their thumbs. We generally trust that the nature of the exaltation - what it grants and the sort of person it settles on - means something.<br /> <br /> Similarly, if someone is rescued from death and tutored by a Deathlord, if he is surrounded by ghostly servants, if he is taught how to twist desires and amplify weaknesses, if he flies at night on the wings of a bat, if he finds great sustenance in living flesh and blood, if he surrounds himself in unnatural cold and darkness, if he lives long enough to see anyone he ever cared about die, then he'll probably struggle to spend his unnatural lifespan rescuing puppies and righting wrongs.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/397623-abyssal-working-for-non-deathlords?p=399306#post399306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is partly because of verisimilitude</div> </div> </div> </div>OK, the v-word does kind of set me off, I have to admit. We all let a lot of implausible stuff slide in order to indulge in fantasy. When I see the v-word, it's usually because someone has latched onto a particular presentation of the system or setting and has chosen, perhaps unconsciously, to be very picky and skeptical about anything that deviates from that presentation. I think people use the v-word to lay claim to a higher standard of &quot;realism&quot; or to imply that they read more carefully and think things through more deeply than others. Alas, it ends up just being a way of rejecting anything that doesn't match the edition or sources that someone happens to prefer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"color:#696969\">When all the world was very young<br /> And mountain magic heavy hung<br /> The supermen would walk in file<br /> Guardians of a loveless isle</span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2010-root","name":"Root","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2010_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1014"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T23:27:19-08:00","id":400070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/397623-abyssal-working-for-non-deathlords?p=399236#post399236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was unaware that the Silver Prince was a line developer!<br /> <br /> Without a lot more context than you've given, all that quote tells us is how the Silver Prince views letting Abyssals run wild and free. That's it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering that it got brought up during discussion of the place and developer sentiment of creating a far freer experience for Abyssals as a character type and the place of Abyssals in the setting. What sounds more like common sense to you. That the developers would provide a flavour piece from a Deathlord as an evocative way to hint at the greater freedom that Abyssals will enjoy that has both setting chapter elements to set the stage for Storyteller &amp; player alike. Along side mechanical reinforcement, and perhaps more importantly, a LACK of rules we've seen in the past like Resonance. Or it's a throwaway line that will quickly be dismissed once they get around to writing the Abyssals splat book.<br /> <br /> Apply common sense in cooperation with the words of intent from the development team vs envision all currently unknown elements of Exalted third edition in the worst possible light because DOOM! I sure know which one I think is more fruitful to engage in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T04:53:43-08:00","id":400176,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I hope is that they still have some sort of interesting mechanic that ensures or attempts to ensure that they do what the Neverborn want'em to do. This is partly because of verisimilitude, which is important to me as a player and as a GM, and partly because aesthetically speaking I really hate the idea that you can sign onto Team Nihilism, get awesome death powers and pseudo-immortality, and there not be really, really powerful strings attached.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sidereals are probably more function-oriented by far than Abyssals, and they never needed such a thing. All they needed was being given powers that ensured they could only do what they were supposed to, and a presentation that made playing a Sidereal within their particular idiom was compelling and credible.<br /> <br /> I imagine that Abyssals might still have their own modified version of the Great Curse to emphasize their deathly, infective nature and also create in-character incentives to adopt all sorts of deathly trappings and create drama around things like having a child or answering to your living name.<br /> <br /> But I don't think they need anything to make them feel like they're doing what the Deathlords (and implicitly the Neverborn) want other than having powers that do those kinds of things and writing a setting that instils the desire to play such characters. They don't need a leash, they just need a sense that the methods and agendas of the Deathlords are reasonably diverse such that almost every character you can play as an Abyssal is fulfilling it one way or the other.<br /> <br /> This also requires the Neverborn, or at least a sense that they're constantly demanding the end of the world, to take a step back, so that such Abyssals can comfortably feel like they're ending the world incrementally, which both enables and removes the pressure from characters who would fulfil and resist. I mean, I still like the idea of Redemption as an option for Abyssals who really no longer want to be harbingers of the eschaton, but I also want Abyssals who are harbingers of the eschaton while still being basically decent people, and more overtly demanding Neverborn and controlling mechanics kill the latter of those. The Neverborn need to back off so one can play a pleasant, cheerful, even noble character who is all for the idea that everything is going to be dust in ten thousand years, without being a lazy bastard.<br /> <br /> The Abyssals can be a fulfilment of the cold, grim desires of the Neverborn, but if the Neverborn are actually in Abyssal stories than it makes it hard to have any story featuring Abyssals that isn't about ending the world <i>right now</i>.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}